---
id: spiced-butter-glazed-wild-pollock
title: Spiced Butter-Glazed Wild Pollock Fillets
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 240

storage:
  fridge_days: 3
  freezer_friendly: false

equipment:
  - air_fryer
---

Submerge the sealed pouches of @wild-pollock-fillet{400%g} in a bowl of cold tap water for ~thaw-time{10%min} until completely pliable.

Remove fillets from packaging and sandwich them between 4 layers of paper towels. Press down firmly with both hands to squeeze out excess processing moisture (crucial to prevent fillets from boiling into watery mush).

Lay pressed fillets on a sheet of parchment paper. Brush tops evenly with melted @unsalted-butter{0.5%tbsp}, then dust with @smoked-paprika{0.5%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.5%tsp}, @onion-powder{0.5%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}, and @dried-dill{0.25%tsp}. (Do not add salt; the brined fillets naturally provide full seasoning).

Transfer the parchment paper directly into the #air-fryer basket. Air fry at 200°C (400°F) for ~cook-time{8%min} (7 to 9 minutes) until opaque and flaking easily at the thickest point.

Immediately squeeze juice from @fresh-lemon{0.5%item} over the hot fillets, and transfer the single cooked portion (240 g cooked yield) into a meal prep container.
